+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+`src/index.ts` already has `applyPatch`, pointer parsing, `cloneJson` (prototype-safe) and `jsonEqual` (member order-insensitive). `createPatch` reuses them. See proposal.md for scope.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** output that `applyPatch` turns into `to`; small patches for localised changes, array insert/remove/move; safe with hostile keys.
+
+**Non-Goals:** the provably shortest patch for arbitrary rearrangements; `copy`/`test` operations.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- **Objects:** iterate own keys (`Object.keys`, `Object.hasOwn`): removes, then recursive changes, then adds. Deterministic order; no operation depends on another.
+- **Arrays, matching:** trim equal prefix/suffix, then compute a longest common subsequence of deeply equal items. LCS items are anchors that never move or change. Alternative (index-by-index comparison) was rejected: an insertion would rewrite every following item.
+- **Arrays, moves:** unmatched `from` items are paired with unmatched equal `to` items; each pair becomes one `move` (RFC 6902 §4.4). A move places the item directly after its predecessor in the target order, so anchors are never disturbed. Alternative remove+add was rejected because it resends the value.
+- **Arrays, in-place changes:** remaining unmatched items lying in the same gap between anchors are paired in order and described recursively, so a modified item yields changes inside it instead of remove+add.
+- **Arrays, emission order:** (1) removals, highest index first; (2) moves, in target order; (3) adds and recursive changes in ascending target index, so earlier indices are final when a later one is used.
+- **Root / type mismatch:** `replace` with path `""` (RFC 6902 §4.3).
+- **Pointers:** tokens escaped `~`→`~0` first, then `/`→`~1` (RFC 6901 §3). Patch values are `cloneJson` copies; `__proto__` is safe because values are read from own properties and copied with `defineProperty`.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [LCS is O(n·m) in comparisons] → trim common prefix/suffix first; acceptable for stored records and payloads.
+- [Output is not guaranteed globally minimal for complex reorderings] → documented as out of scope; correctness (round trip) is always guaranteed and tested with randomised round trips.
+- [Inputs that are not JSON (undefined, NaN, functions) are unspecified] → out of scope, as for `applyPatch`.
